            <ArticleTitle>Painful extremities and neurological disorder in essential thrombocythaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>372-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Six of 20 patients with essential thrombocythaemia had neurological features and 8 had peripheral vascular symptoms. Four had cerebrovascular ischaemia or stroke and 3 had gangrene. Pain in the extremities may be a striking symptom in this disorder.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
